		</section>

		<section class="section">
			<SectionHeader Title="Detection" Meta="DELIBERATELY ADVERSARIAL" />
			<div class="concept-list">
				<Concept
					ID="coach-detection"
					Title="The pattern table is one input, not the authority"
					Diagram="Per pipeline (segments split on ; / && / || / &): normalize first (heredoc bodies stripped, subshells and backticks wrapped, variables marked, $IFS to space, quote layers removed, leading command word lowercased), then the pattern rows (24 built-in DEFAULT_PATTERNS; user rows appended, no built-in duplicates - fail-loud), an intent-marker scan, a craft library for the obfuscated variants, and the catch-all - any write-intent marker on a non-/dev/null path lands as write, so novel zero-day forms still count."
				>
					<p>
						Exemptions are checked per pipeline AFTER normalization.
						An exempt head dominates its pipe (<code>git diff &gt; patch.txt</code> is exempt).
						A bare <code>echo x &gt; tracked.md</code> is not.
					</p>
					<p>
						Five classes: <strong>write, read, search, discovery, control</strong>.
						Class-priority resolution applies across chained segments
						(<code>cat a; sed -i ...</code> counts once, as write).
					</p>
				</Concept>
			</div>
			<div class="table-wrap">
				<table class="table">
					<thead>
						<tr>
							<th>Pattern (representative rows of the 24)</th>
							<th>Class</th>
							<th>Mapped tool</th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						{Patterns.map((Row) => (
							<tr>
								<td>{Row.Pattern}</td>
								<td>
									<strong>{Row.Class}</strong>
								</td>
								<td set:html={Mention(Row.Tool)} />
							</tr>
						))}
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="section">
			<SectionHeader Title="The dynamic instruction engine" Meta="LIVE-FETCHED TOOL TABLE" />
			<div class="concept-list">
				<Concept
					ID="coach-engine"
					Title="Every note names the correct tool with its LIVE registry data"
					Diagram={"ctx.tools.schemas() fetched through the same injection the model's own tools arrive by: the tool name, the FIRST SENTENCE of its description (<= 120 chars, parenthesis-aware) and the primary parameter key (parameters.properties[0]). " + "Tier 1/3 fetch per note; tier 2 caches for sectionTtl (20) judged calls and rebuilds on tools/change. " + "Any fetch failure degrades to the static STATIC_TOOL_LINES table and logs schema fetch failed -> static fallback; fetchLive: false is the escape hatch (static only, no failure line)."}
				>
					<p>
						Template fills are single-pass.
						User data is escaped before insertion.
						Composed output never gains an unfilled placeholder.
					</p>
				</Concept>
			</div>
			<p class="section-kicker">
				<BrandIcon Name="terminal" />The tier-1 note, placeholders filled
			</p>
			<CodeBlock Language="text" Source={NoteFirst.join("\n")} />
			<p class="section-kicker">
				<BrandIcon Name="terminal" />The tier-2 persistent section, placeholders filled
			</p>
			<CodeBlock Language="text" Source={NotePersistent.join("\n")} />
		</section>

		<section class="section">
			<SectionHeader Title="The Config" Meta="SCHEMA + DEFAULTS AT LOAD - EVERY CELL VOLATILE" />
			<div class="concept-list">
				<Concept
					ID="coach-config-schema"
					Title="The exported Config schema"
					Diagram={"The factory's standalone Schema(false, {...}) helper validating and filling every default at load; every cell volatile - a flip lands on the next judged call. " + "Fail-loud validation in apply: threshold >= 1, window >= threshold, cooldown >= 1, escalateThreshold >= threshold, cleanWindow >= 1, enforceThreshold >= 1, maxSectionTools 1-24, sectionTtl >= 1, every row pattern compiles + tool non-empty, no built-in duplicates, notes templates non-empty."}
				>
					<p>
						New patch entries are declared with <code>insert:</code>. Full example:
					</p>
				</Concept>
			</div>
			<CodeBlock
				Language="yaml"
				Source={[
					"- insert:",
					"      - id: hook-dsh-tool-coach",
					'        name: "@playform/hook-dsh-tool-coach"',
					"        config:",
					"            log: true",
					"            logFile: ~/.dsh/hook-dsh-tool-coach.log",
					"            enabled: true # the MASTER switch",
					"            judgeTools: [bash, pwsh] # the dedicated tools are never judged",
					"            threshold: 3 # tier-1 strikes per class",
					"            window: 8 # the sliding window of judged calls",
					"            cooldown: 10 # judged calls between tier-1 notes",
					"            escalateThreshold: 6 # tier-2 section on",
					"            cleanWindow: 12 # clean calls that clear the section",
					"            enforce: off # 'off' | 'write' | 'all' - tier-3 denies",
					"            enforceThreshold: 4 # per-class strikes since the last note",
					"            fetchLive: true # the live ctx.tools.schemas() fetch",
					"            maxSectionTools: 8 # the tier-2 tool-table row cap",
					"            sectionTtl: 20 # judged calls the section text is cached for",
				].join("\n")}
			/>
			<div class="table-wrap">
				<table class="table">
					<thead>
						<tr>
							<th>Field</th>
							<th>Type</th>
							<th>Default</th>
							<th>Meaning</th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						{Config.map((Row) => (
							<tr>
								<td>
									<strong>{Row.Field}</strong>
								</td>
								<td>{Row.Type}</td>
								<td set:html={Mention(Row.Default)} />
								<td set:html={Mention(Row.Meaning)} />
							</tr>
						))}
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="section">
			<SectionHeader Title="In Action" Meta="ONE COACHED STREAM" />
			<div class="concept-list">
				<Concept
					ID="coach-in-action-stream"
					Title="A cat stream, judged and coached"
					Diagram="The model reading file content through the terminal - cat config.json four times inside the window - each offense logging its tier-0 line silently, the fourth crossing the threshold and firing the tier-1 note with the LIVE-fetched read description; six total offenses escalating the persistent section; twelve clean calls clearing it."
				>
					<p>
						The model reads file content through the terminal - <code>cat config.json</code> four times inside the window.
						Each offense logs its tier-0 line silently.
						The fourth crosses the threshold, the note fires.
					</p>
				</Concept>
			</div>
			<p class="section-kicker">
				<BrandIcon Name="swap" />The ledger lines for the stream
			</p>
			<div class="code-block">{LedgerExcerpt.join("\n")}</div>
			<div class="concept-list">
				<Concept
					ID="coach-in-action-deny"
					Title="The tier-3 deny, when enforce is armed"
					Diagram={"With enforce: 'write' and the write-class strikes at the enforce threshold, the pre-execute listener returns {kind: 'deny', reason} - the reason being the NOTE_DENIED text - and logs denied bash write <pattern> -> use edit. " + "The deny resets the note counters; the denied call still flows through post-execute, so counting continues."}
				>
					<p>
						With <code>enforce: 'write'</code> and the write-class strikes at the enforce threshold, the call is blocked.
						The deny reason IS the lesson:
					</p>
				</Concept>
			</div>
			<p class="section-kicker">
				<BrandIcon Name="swap" />The deny reason the model sees
			</p>
			<CodeBlock Language="text" Source={NoteDenied.join("\n")} />
		</section>

		<section class="section">
			<SectionHeader Title="The Ledger" Meta="ONE LOG PER MODULE" />
			<div class="concept-list">
				<Concept
					ID="coach-ledger-log"
					Title="The ten strings are the contract"
					Diagram="One log per module - logFile (default ~/.dsh/hook-dsh-tool-coach.log) - the ten strings byte-exact with the hook-dsh-tool-coach: logger prefix (the factory's Append layer; each line [ISO] <message> in the file): offense, strike, cooldown suppressed, escalated persistent section, persistent section cleared, section rebuilt, denied, exempt, schema fetch failed, disabled."
				>
					<p>
						The durable ledger file carries the same strings in <code>[ISO] &lt;message&gt;</code> form.
						The strings below are the module's composed messages, byte-exact.
						The rebuild line logs one line per path - the smoke's byte-exact forms{" "}
						<code>section rebuilt (ttl 2)</code> and <code>section rebuilt (tools/change)</code>.
					</p>
				</Concept>
			</div>
			<div class="code-block">{LedgerStrings.join("\n")}</div>
		</section>

		<!-- The known limits: the documented gaps, stated as they are. -->
		<section class="section">
			<SectionHeader Title="Known limits" Meta="THE DOCUMENTED GAPS" />
			<p class="page-hero__sub" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-md)">
				<strong>The coach teaches; it does not rewrite.</strong>
			</p>
			<p class="page-hero__sub" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-md)">
				No tier modifies the model's history.
				Tier 1 appends a note to the current turn's <code>additionalContexts</code>.
				Tier 2 appends a section to the system prompt.
				Tier 3 blocks the call before execution - the past turns are never touched.
			</p>
			<p class="page-hero__sub" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-md)">
				<strong>The live fetch can fail, gracefully.</strong>
			</p>
			<p class="page-hero__sub" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-md)">
				A throwing <code>ctx.tools.schemas()</code> degrades to the static <code>STATIC_TOOL_LINES</code> table.
				It logs <code>schema fetch failed -&gt; static fallback</code>.
				The waterfall continues - a note never fails a waterfall.
			</p>
			<p class="page-hero__sub" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-md)">
				<code>fetchLive: false</code> uses the static table unconditionally with no failure line.
			</p>
			<p class="page-hero__sub" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-md)">
				<strong>Detection is heuristic by design.</strong>
			</p>
			<p class="page-hero__sub" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-md)">
				The catch-all keeps the recall high (novel write forms still count).
				Exemptions keep the precision acceptable (builds, tests, git, package managers, file lifecycle).
				The balance is documented in the smoke battery's exempt cases, including the <code>cat | jq</code> carve-out dedup.
			</p>
		</section>

